        "si_used": true,
        "procedure": "Due to the air-sensitivity of CrCl2, all procedures up to the final crystallisation were carried out under argon or nitrogen using a Braun glovebox or standard Schlenk technique, with dried solvents. A mixture of CrCl2 (0.124 g, 1.00 mmol), NaN3 (0.110 g, 1.69 mmol) and N-methyldiethanolamine (373 μL, 3.55 mmol) in acetonitrile (15 mL) was stirred at room temperature for 50 min. After addition of Dy(NO3)3·6H2O (200 mg, 0.44 mmol) and pivalic acid (400 mg, 3.91 mmol) the mixture was stirred for another 10 min before addition of dichloromethane (10 mL). The mixture was stirred at room temperature overnight (13 h). The solution was filtered and exposed to air; slow evaporation of the solvent gave pink crystals of 1.",
