      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Octanuclear Cr4Dy4 cluster is an SMM: χT decreases from 64.23 cm3 K mol−1 at room temperature to 35.9 cm3 K mol−1 at 1.8 K, indicating intramolecular antiferromagnetic interactions and/or Dy Stark-level depopulation. Slow magnetization relaxation occurs below 5 K; Arrhenius analysis gives an energy barrier of 15 K with τ0 = 1.9(1)×10−7 s. Single-crystal micro-SQUID measurements show hysteresis (0.2 T at 0.04 K) with magnetization steps and sweep-rate-dependent loops.",
